<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  REV Grant Administration - the model-driven app the process owner works in.

  WHY PHASE 1 NEEDS AN APP
  Three approved requirements have no other surface. FR-017 needs the process owner to edit
  thresholds herself; FR-018 needs her to override an automated status and have the override
  recorded against her name; FR-019 and FR-020 need a Borderline working list and a separate
  rejected list. The saved queries that already ship with this solution exist to be shown
  somewhere, and this is that somewhere. The trustee portal is a different surface entirely
  (Code App, Phase 3, ADR-003) and is not in this release.

  ROLE ASSOCIATION IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY BELOW.
  <AppModuleRoles /> stays empty because app sharing is per-environment configuration, not a
  solution component (TAD section 12). provisioning/dataverse/share-apps.ps1 associates this
  app with REV Admin and REV Service Automation at post_deploy, looking the roles up by name.

  ACCESSIBILITY
  A model-driven app inherits the platform's own accessibility behaviour, so the WCAG 2.1 AA
  obligation here (TAD section 8) falls on the parts this solution authors: every custom column
  carries a meaningful display name and a description, both of which are already present in the
  Entity.xml files, and the Setting editing surface conveys nothing by colour alone - a
  threshold's value is read from the Value column as text, not from any styling.

  PACKAGING CAVEAT - this file and AppModuleSiteMap.xml are hand-authored. App module and
  sitemap XML is the component type whose unpacked layout varies most between pac CLI versions.
  Replace both with the output of a real `pac solution unpack` as soon as a DEV environment
  exists. Recorded in Dev Summary section 7.
-->
<AppModule>
  <appmoduleid>{d4f6a8b0-4001-4e5c-8f77-0a1b2c3d4e31}</appmoduleid>
  <name>REV Grant Administration</name>
  <uniquename>rev_grantadministration</uniquename>
  <url>rev_grantadministration</url>
  <descriptions>
    <description description="Administration surface for the grant application process. Review new applications, see how a circumstance score was reached, override an automated status with a recorded reason, and maintain the scoring configuration the board sets." languagecode="1033" />
  </descriptions>
  <LocalizedNames>
    <LocalizedName description="REV Grant Administration" languagecode="1033" />
  </LocalizedNames>
  <clienttype>4</clienttype>
  <navigationtype>1</navigationtype>
  <formfactor>2</formfactor>
  <isdefault>0</isdefault>
  <isfeatured>0</isfeatured>
  <statecode>0</statecode>
  <iscustomizable>1</iscustomizable>
  <introducedversion>1.0.0.0</introducedversion>
  <IntroducedVersion>1.0.0.0</IntroducedVersion>
  <AppModuleRoles />
  <AppModuleComponents>
